# Video demo section is mandatory on Elementor PRs

Before running `gh pr create` or `gh pr edit` on `elementor/elementor` or
`elementor/elementor-pro`, read [SKILL.md](mdc:.cursor/skills/video-proof-demo/SKILL.md)
and author the `## Video demo` section yourself. This applies to `/pr`,
`create-ship-deploy`, Cloud Agents, and manual PR creation.

- Order in the body: `## Summary` → `## Test plan` → `## Video demo` → `## Jira`
- Every UI PR gets one Where / Steps / Pass / Fail block; bugs add a `**Broken:**` caption line
- Never script the broken behaviour — `playground-preview.yml` installs only the fixed PR build
- No useful UI → keep the heading with `#skip_video` + one sentence why
- Never leave placeholders and never ask the user to write the section
- Steps use visible in-app labels only — no file paths, GitHub, or CI references

The `## Video demo` section is read by the demo recorder, which drives Playwright
against the PR's `playground-preview` deployment. Write it for that runner, not
for human reviewers — they read Summary and Test plan.
